**How to implement.** The reference pipeline reads its labels through the naming template, and the label regular expressions go (001 §J 'It replaces `MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed` and its `experimentRegex`'; 001 §R; 001 §T 'From section 8: `git grep -n -F "experimentRegex" -- Berreman/` finds nothing', which this step makes true). `MuellerReconstructionTests`' numbers are unchanged. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`: (1) Deleted: `experimentRegex` and `objectRegex` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:experimentRegex`, `:objectRegex`), the `MuellerExperimentLabel` extension holding `parsed` (`:parsed`), `ParsedExperiment` (`:ParsedExperiment`), `ParsedObject` (`:ParsedObject`) and `MuellerLabelToken` (`:MuellerLabelToken`), whose only readers are each other, `buildDesign` and `MuellerReconstructionTests` (the census names no other), with the doc and comment lines that describe them; and `open System.Text.RegularExpressions` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:3`), which nothing else reads. The file opens `Kit`, `Setups` and `NamingTemplates`. (2) `MuellerExperimentLabel` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MuellerExperimentLabel`) gains `member this.nameText : NameText`, its text as a name (step 269); its doc says a label reads through `NamingTemplate.standard` (step 267). (3) After `MatrixKind` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixKind`), `type NameReading with`, the reference pipeline's reading of a label, moved from `ParsedExperiment` with its rules unchanged: `member this.family : Family` takes a part as the circular family when its text contains `CPL` (the reference `canonical_polarizer`), over the source part (`tryFindPart (PrepSlotRole (SlotPosition 1))`) and the analyzer part (`AnalyzerSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)`), an absent part being linear; `member this.objectRotation : Angle * MatrixKind` takes the objects as the reading's `ObjectSlotRole` parts that have an angle of their position, in position order: none is `Angle.zero, Air`; one is its angle and, by its text upper-cased (`ToUpperInvariant`), `Qz` for `QZ`, `Lr` for `LR` and `Air` otherwise; two or more are the first's angle and `QzLrProduct`; `member this.matrixKind : MatrixKind` and `member this.objectPhi : Angle` are its halves. (4) `buildDesign` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:buildDesign`) keeps a row whose label `NamingTemplate.standard.readName r.experiment.nameText` reads with a `matrixKind` equal to `kind`, a label the template does not read being never kept, and otherwise filters as it does; its doc says so. Every science label of the lab's files reads (`CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2`, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL-2`, …), so every design holds the same rows in the same order. The one reading that differs is a darkness label such as `CPL-(Darkness)-LP-2`, which `parsed` read as `Air` and the template does not read; no design selects `Air`. (5) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit`. Its fact `parseExperiment decodes CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL and the +90 / -90 object rotation is inert (R(2 phi) invariance)` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:559`) becomes `the standard naming template reads CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL as the CPL-CPL family and the QZ LR product at phi 90, and the +90 / -90 object rotation is inert (R(2 phi) invariance)`: the label is read by `NamingTemplate.standard.readName (MuellerExperimentLabel "CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL").nameText`, an `Error` failing the fact with its `describe`, and its assertions are unchanged. In the section 7.2 fact, `prepareRow` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:945`) takes `phi` as that reading's `objectPhi` in the same way. Tests. `NamingTemplateTests` (it opens `MuellerReconstruction`) gains `a lab label's reading names its reference family, matrix kind and object angle`: `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL` is `CplCpl`, `QzLrProduct` and 90°; `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL` `CplCpl`, `Air` and 0°; `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2` `LpCpl`, `Lr` and 90°; `CPL-(QZ#45)-LP-2` `CplLp`, `Qz` and 45°; and `LP-(QZ#0)-LP-2R` `LpLp`, `Qz` and 0°. `MuellerReconstructionTests`' facts pass with their numbers unchanged, `buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)` and the section 7.2 fact included.

**Acceptance.** After the reference pipeline reads its labels through the template, `experimentRegex`, `objectRegex`, `MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed`, `ParsedExperiment`, `ParsedObject` and `MuellerLabelToken` MUST be gone and `git grep -n -F "experimentRegex" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing, and `buildDesign` and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST read labels through `NamingTemplate.standard` and the moved `NameReading.family`, `matrixKind` and `objectPhi`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a lab label's reading names its reference family, matrix kind and object angle`, the count rising by 1; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its fact renamed to `the standard naming template reads CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL as the CPL-CPL family and the QZ LR product at phi 90, and the +90 / -90 object rotation is inert (R(2 phi) invariance)` and its numbers unchanged; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.
